<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Contact in a transient analysis: quasi-static load ramp</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      The ContactPatchTest2d model solved as a TRANSIENT analysis instead of a static one. This
      is the first testcase to run contact through StepTransNonLin at all; every other contact
      test goes through StepStaticNonLin.

      The pressure is ramped linearly to 1e6 Pa over a time about 32 times the column's
      fundamental period, so inertia stays negligible and the final state must reproduce the
      static answer: contact pressure 1e6 Pa, resultant 2e6 N, penetration -p/eps_N. It does, to
      0.04 %. Ramping faster leaves the structure ringing and the error grows smoothly with the
      load rate, which is what makes this a quasi-static convergence check rather than a single
      lucky number.

      What is actually being checked is that the contact machinery is reached and behaves in the
      transient solve step: the residual there is built as f - K*u from the same non-Newton
      STIFFNESS matrices as in the static path, so the split should carry over unchanged, and
      the per-time-step contact reporting should follow the deformation.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactTransient2d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="plane">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis>
      <transient>
        <numSteps>70</numSteps>
        <deltaT>2e-3</deltaT>
      </transient>
    </analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="planeStrain">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="transient_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the lateral rigid-body mode only. Its y support comes
               exclusively from the contact interface, which is the point of the test. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- ramp to full load over the first half of the run, then hold -->
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6*min(t/1e-1,1)"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
